## Codebase Discoveries
TorchSpec DFlash2 adds selector cross-entropy over teacher-forced adjacent transitions to shared DFlash training. When gold is absent from draft-logit top-K, training replaces the weakest candidate with gold. Serving never inserts gold.

Public serving has no per-target-layer fc_norm. Selector codebooks use full target-vocabulary token IDs. Candidate top-K parity requires a finite positive output multiplier, and the softcap must be finite and positive when set.

Strict conversion rejects all missing or unexpected DFlash2 state keys. The only exception is embed_tokens.weight when target_model_path is present, because the converter immediately replaces it. Serving exports omit embedding and LM head and emit bare selector codebook names.

FULL_SHARD scalar reduction must use a local CUDA scalar, not a DTensor scalar. Only data-parallel rank zero writes the online artifact, and ranks exchange writer errors before returning.

The exact run has 375 updates and saves iteration 376 because metadata records the next iteration. The serving gate's prompt-only acceptance lengths were 2.909090909090909, 5.333333333333333, and 8.0.

